.TH "HTMLSLOTELEMENT.ASSIGN" "3JS" "September 11, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLSlotElement.assign \- HTMLSlotElement: assign() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]assign()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]HTMLSlotElement\f[R] interface sets the slot\(cqs \f[I]manually
assigned nodes\f[R] to an ordered set of slottables.
The manually assigned nodes set is initially empty until nodes are
assigned using \f[CR]assign()\f[R].
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] Manual assignments determine the slot\(cqs displayed
content only when the shadow tree has been created with the
\f[CR]slotAssignment: \(dqmanual\(dq\f[R] option.
In a shadow tree using named (automatic) assignment, calling
\f[CR]assign()\f[R] still updates the slot\(cqs manually assigned nodes,
but does not override named assignment.
.RE
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
assign()
assign(node1)
assign(node1, node2)
assign(node1, node2, /* \&..., */ nodeN)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]node1\f[R], \&..., \f[B]nodeN\f[R]
A set of \f[CR]Element\f[R] or \f[CR]Text\f[R] nodes.
Passing zero arguments clears the slot\(cqs manually assigned nodes, and
its fallback content is displayed.
Fallback content is also displayed when no nodes have been assigned or
all assigned nodes have been removed from the shadow host.
.RS
.PP
Removing a node from the shadow host preserves its manual assignment, so
reinserting it into the host restores its slot assignment unless the
manual assignment has been changed using \f[CR]assign()\f[R].
.RE
.SS Return value
None (\f[CR]undefined\f[R]).
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Displaying assigned nodes and fallback content
In this example, the \f[CR]assign()\f[R] method is used to display one
of two panels.
Click a panel button to assign that panel to the slot, or click \(lqShow
fallback\(rq to clear the assignment and display the slot\(cqs fallback
content.
Switching panels or clearing the assignment does not remove the panels
from the shadow host.
.PP
To compare clearing an assignment with removing a node, first display a
panel, then click \(lqRemove assigned panel\(rq.
This removes the panel from the shadow host without calling
\f[CR]assign()\f[R].
The fallback content should appear automatically.
Clicking any other button first restores any removed panels to the
shadow host.
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]div\f[R]>
  <\f[B]button\f[R] id=\(dqshow\-first\(dq>Show first panel</\f[B]button\f[R]>
  <\f[B]button\f[R] id=\(dqshow\-second\(dq>Show second panel</\f[B]button\f[R]>
  <\f[B]button\f[R] id=\(dqshow\-fallback\(dq>Show fallback</\f[B]button\f[R]>
  <\f[B]button\f[R] id=\(dqremove\-panel\(dq>Remove assigned panel</\f[B]button\f[R]>
</\f[B]div\f[R]>

<\f[B]div\f[R] id=\(dqpanels\(dq>
  <\f[B]tab\-panel\f[R]><\f[B]p\f[R]>This is the first panel.</\f[B]p\f[R]></\f[B]tab\-panel\f[R]>
  <\f[B]tab\-panel\f[R]><\f[B]p\f[R]>This is the second panel.</\f[B]p\f[R]></\f[B]tab\-panel\f[R]>
</\f[B]div\f[R]>
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]function\f[R] updateDisplayTab(elem, tabIdx) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] shadow = elem.shadowRoot;
  \f[B]const\f[R] slot = shadow.querySelector(\(dqslot\(dq);
  \f[B]const\f[R] panels = elem.querySelectorAll(\(dqtab\-panel\(dq);
  \f[B]if\f[R] (panels.length && tabIdx && tabIdx <= panels.length) {
    slot.assign(panels[tabIdx \- 1]);
  } \f[B]else\f[R] {
    \f[I]// Clear any previous assignment to display the slot\(aqs fallback content.\f[R]
    slot.assign();
  }
}

\f[B]const\f[R] host = document.querySelector(\(dq#panels\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] panels = host.querySelectorAll(\(dqtab\-panel\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] shadow = host.attachShadow({
  mode: \(dqopen\(dq,
  slotAssignment: \(dqmanual\(dq,
});
shadow.innerHTML = \(ga
  <slot>
    <p>This is the fallback content. No panel is assigned.</p>
  </slot>
\(ga;
\f[B]const\f[R] slot = shadow.querySelector(\(dqslot\(dq);

\f[B]function\f[R] restorePanels() {
  \f[B]for\f[R] (\f[B]let\f[R] i = panels.length \- 1; i >= 0; i\-\-) {
    \f[B]if\f[R] (panels[i].parentNode !== host) {
      host.insertBefore(panels[i], panels[i + 1] ?? \f[B]null\f[R]);
    }
  }
}

document.querySelector(\(dq#show\-first\(dq).addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  restorePanels();
  updateDisplayTab(host, 1);
});

document.querySelector(\(dq#show\-second\(dq).addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  restorePanels();
  updateDisplayTab(host, 2);
});

document.querySelector(\(dq#show\-fallback\(dq).addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  restorePanels();
  updateDisplayTab(host, 0);
});

document.querySelector(\(dq#remove\-panel\(dq).addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]for\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] panel \f[B]of\f[R] slot.assignedNodes()) {
    \f[I]// Remove the node without clearing its manual assignment.\f[R]
    panel.remove();
  }
});
.EE
.SS Result
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]Element.attachShadow()\f[R]
